          For walking, a treadmill and a pavement are closer than most people expect. The biggest
          difference between treadmill running and road running — air resistance — hardly applies
          at 3 or 4 mph. What remains is a set of smaller differences: the ground moves under you
          rather than you over it, the surface is perfectly flat and even, some people shorten
          their stride or look down, a narrow moving deck asks something different of balance,
          and step counters and distance figures behave differently indoors. None of these stop a
