        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Walking on a treadmill is not identical to walking outside, but it
            is close, and it is real exercise.</strong> Wind barely matters at walking pace; the
            differences that do matter are the flat surface, a moving belt, balance on a narrow
            deck, how trackers count steps, and the mental side.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Let go of the rails, add a little incline and some variety, use a fan, and walk outside
            when you can for the terrain and the daylight. For sessions that build in those
            changes, see our
            <a href="/treadmill-walking-workouts/" class="text-[#5AA9FF] font-bold no-underline">treadmill walking workouts</a>.
          </p>
